{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Sync CONTRIBUTING.md with content structure",
  "description": "When content files (.md in content/), data files (.yaml under data/ and its subfolders), or configuration files (config/_default/*.yaml) change, asks the agent to update the \"Où se trouvent les fichiers\" section in .github/CONTRIBUTING.md so the documentation stays in sync with the actual site structure.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "content/**/*.md",
      "data/**/*.yaml",
      "config/_default/*.yaml"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A source file in the repository was just edited. Check whether the \"Où se trouvent les fichiers\" section in `.github/CONTRIBUTING.md` needs to be updated to reflect this change.\n\nSpecifically:\n1. Read the current list of files under `content/`, `data/` (including its subfolders such as `data/fr/`, `data/en/`, `data/metadata/`), and the configuration files under `config/_default/` to understand the actual site structure.\n2. Compare it with the tables in the \"Où se trouvent les fichiers\" section of `.github/CONTRIBUTING.md`.\n3. If a content page was added, renamed, or removed, update the corresponding table in CONTRIBUTING.md (add a row, remove a row, or fix the filename).\n4. If a new section folder appeared under `content/`, add a new subsection with its own table.\n5. If a data file (anywhere under `data/`) was added or removed, update the relevant mention in CONTRIBUTING.md.\n6. If a configuration file under `config/_default/` changed in a way that affects the documented structure, update the relevant mention in CONTRIBUTING.md.\n7. If nothing changed structurally (e.g. only text inside an existing page was edited), do NOT modify CONTRIBUTING.md.\n\nThe source of truth is always the actual files on disk — CONTRIBUTING.md is the documentation that must follow."
  }
}